## Implementation Matches Official Documentation

According to the Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects:
- ✓ Install `@vercel/analytics` package
- ✓ Import `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/react`
- ✓ Add `<Analytics />` component to root layout file (`app/layout.js`)
- ✓ Place component inside `<body>` tag

All requirements are met.

## Files Modified

- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Regenerated to ensure dependency lock consistency

## Next Steps for Deployment

To complete the setup and start collecting analytics data:

1. **Enable Analytics in Vercel Dashboard**
   - Navigate to your Vercel project dashboard
   - Go to Analytics section in the sidebar
   - Click "Enable" button

2. **Deploy to Vercel**
   - Run `vercel deploy` or push to your connected Git repository
   - Vercel will automatically detect the Analytics component

3. **Verify Data Collection**
   - After deployment, visit your site
   - Check browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`
   - View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard

## Notes

- The implementation uses the latest version (2.0.1) of @vercel/analytics
- Speed Insights is also configured (`@vercel/speed-insights@2.0.0`)
- Custom event tracking is available via the imported `track` function
- Analytics only works on Vercel deployments (not in local development)
- No additional configuration or environment variables required
